From d4d53c050bc5a9fd43980c1895909e20436d8ff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PabloBenario <pablo.benario@ug.uchile.cl>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 10:34:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Render [INCOMPLETE] breakdown below verdict line

When the Incomplete message carries multi-line content (e.g. an encoded
breakdown of per-reason incomplete-case counts from qcheck-inc's
QCheck_alcotest bridge), render the lines after the first indented under
the verdict name column (16 spaces = left_gutter + left_tag).

The lines are wrapped in an explicit @[<v>...@] vbox so @, acts as a hard
cut instead of being packed together by Format's default margin logic.

Single-line messages (e.g. the existing incomplete_in_test case
'failwith "TODO: not yet implemented"') hit the no-render branch and are
visually unchanged.

New regression test incomplete_breakdown_in_test exercises the multi-line
path. Its committed .expected file pins the exact column layout; the
existing incomplete_in_test.expected continues to pass unchanged.
