Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Add per-test verdict suffix hook

Expose a ref (Pp.current_test_suffix) plus a top-level helper
(Alcotest.set_test_suffix) that test runners can use to attach a short
stats string to the current test's verdict line. The patched `event`
arm for `Result reads and clears the ref when rendering, appends the
suffix after the test doc (3-space gap), and reserves the suffix width
when computing available_width so the doc truncates earlier if needed.

The qcheck-alcotest bridge uses this to render 'N passed, M incomplete,
K failed' inline on every test's verdict line, including clean [OK]
runs where no exception is raised.

Minimal surface: one ref, one setter, one extra optional arg to
pp_result_full. Unused (nothing calls set_test_suffix) the feature is
dormant: the ref stays None, the suffix branch is skipped.
