+++ b/INCOMPLETE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,189 @@
+# The `[INCOMPLETE]` Patch
+
+This is a patched fork of [mirage/alcotest](https://github.com/mirage/alcotest)
+on branch `qcheck-inc-incomplete`, based on tag `1.9.1`. It adds a fourth
+verdict tag, `[INCOMPLETE]` (yellow), to the alcotest runner.
+
+The feature stands on its own as a plain-alcotest addition — there is no
+dependency on QCheck or any other external library. The e2e regression
+test inside this repository uses only vanilla alcotest.
+
+## What the patch adds
+
+Upstream alcotest classifies every test result as one of three outcomes:
+
+- `[OK]` — the test ran and passed.
+- `[FAIL]` — the test ran and failed.
+- `[SKIP]` — the test was skipped.
+
+This patch adds a fourth:
+
+- `[INCOMPLETE]` — the test reached a point that is not yet implemented,
+  signalled via `failwith "TODO:..."`. It is **not** counted as a failure,
+  does **not** contribute to a nonzero exit code, but **is** counted in the
+  summary's "N tests run" total.
+
+`[INCOMPLETE]` lets a test suite distinguish "I haven't written this yet"
+from "this is broken", without the placeholder turning green (which would
+risk forgetting it).
+
+## Trigger
+
+`[INCOMPLETE]` is produced by exactly one convention: **a test raises
+`Failure s` where `s` starts with the literal prefix `"TODO:"`**.
+
+Typically:
+
+```ocaml
+let not_yet () = failwith "TODO: implement the sad path"
+
+let () =
+  Alcotest.run "my_suite"
+    [ "unit", [ Alcotest.test_case "sad path" `Quick not_yet ] ]
+```
+
+Rendered output:
+
+```
+  [INCOMPLETE]  unit          0   sad path.
+
+Test Successful in … 1 tests run.
+```
+
+…with exit code 0.
+
+`failwith` is `Stdlib`, so there is no import, no new alcotest value, no
+new exception. A stock (unpatched) alcotest would treat the same call as
+`[FAIL]` with exit 1.
+
+## End-to-end trace
+
+1. The test body calls `failwith "TODO: ..."`, which raises
+   `Stdlib.Failure "TODO: ..."`.
+2. `Core.protect_test` in `src/alcotest-engine/core.ml:192` has a
+   `when`-guard that catches this exact prefix before the generic
+   `Failure s` arm:
+
+   ```ocaml
+   | Failure s when String.is_prefix ~affix:"TODO:" s -> `Incomplete s
+   ```
+
+   The matched message is carried on the variant.
+3. `Run_result.t` in `src/alcotest-engine/model.ml:56` includes the new
+   case `` `Incomplete of string ``. `is_failure` (line 59-61) returns
+   `false` for it, so exit-code accounting treats it as not-a-failure.
+   `Core.has_run` (`core.ml:177`) returns `true`, so it counts toward
+   the "N tests run" summary.
+4. `src/alcotest-engine/pp.ml` renders it:
+   - colour `` `Yellow `` (line 29)
+   - label `"INCOMPLETE"` (line 37)
+   - error body suppressed (line 59)
+   - `tag_of_result` mapping (line 109)
+   - compact-mode character `'I'` (line 123)
+5. `src/alcotest-engine/pp_intf.ml:85` extends the `tag` polymorphic
+   variant accordingly.
+6. The run summary and exit decision treat Incomplete tests as neutral,
+   i.e. the run exits 0 if no `[FAIL]` occurred.
+
+## Files touched vs. tag 1.9.1
+
+| File                                                    | Change                                                                                                       |
+|---------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| `src/alcotest-engine/model.ml`                          | Adds `` `Incomplete of string `` to `Run_result.t`; excludes it from `is_failure`.                           |
+| `src/alcotest-engine/core.ml`                           | `has_run` returns true for `` `Incomplete _ ``; `protect_test` when-guard routes `Failure "TODO:..."` to it. |
+| `src/alcotest-engine/pp_intf.ml`                        | Adds `` `Incomplete `` to the `tag` polymorphic variant.                                                     |
+| `src/alcotest-engine/pp.ml`                             | Five branches: colour, label, error-body suppression, `tag_of_result` mapping, compact-mode character.       |
+| `test/e2e/alcotest/passing/incomplete_in_test.ml`       | Minimal regression test (vanilla alcotest — no QCheck).                                                      |
+| `test/e2e/alcotest/passing/incomplete_in_test.expected` | Sanitised expected output for the `runtest` diff alias.                                                      |
+| `test/e2e/alcotest/passing/dune.inc`                    | Regenerated by `gen_dune_rules.exe` to wire the new test in.                                                 |
+
+Roughly 11 lines of feature code plus the e2e fixture. No public
+identifier is added, removed, or renamed — the API surface is identical
+to stock alcotest.
+
+## Semantic contract
+
+| Aspect                  | Behaviour                                                                                                                          |
+|-------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| Trigger                 | `failwith "TODO:<anything>"` inside a test body (stdlib only).                                                                     |
+| Rendered tag            | Yellow `[INCOMPLETE]` in verbose mode, `'I'` in compact mode.                                                                      |
+| Error body              | Suppressed (same as Ok / Skip / Todo).                                                                                             |
+| Exit code               | Neutral — does NOT contribute to a nonzero exit.                                                                                   |
+| Summary counter         | Included in "N tests run".                                                                                                         |
+| Public API              | Unchanged vs. stock alcotest.                                                                                                      |
+| Stock-alcotest fallback | `failwith "TODO:..."` falls into the generic `Failure` arm → `[FAIL]` + exit 1. Silent behavioural degradation, not a build error. |
+
+## E2E regression test
+
+The canonical guard is `test/e2e/alcotest/passing/incomplete_in_test.ml`:
+
+```ocaml
+let () =
+  let open Alcotest in
+  let id () = () in
+  let todo () = failwith "TODO: not yet implemented" in
+  run __FILE__
+    [
+      ( "test-a",
+        [
+          test_case "Run test case" `Quick id;
+          test_case "TODO test case" `Quick todo;
+        ] );
+    ]
+```
+
+The accompanying `incomplete_in_test.expected` asserts:
+
+```
+  [OK]          test-a          0   Run test case.
+  [INCOMPLETE]  test-a          1   TODO test case.
+
+Test Successful in <test-duration>s. 2 tests run.
+```
+
+Run it alongside the rest of the passing-e2e suite:
+
+```sh
+dune runtest test/e2e/alcotest/passing
+```
+
+A silent pass means the when-guard is wired correctly. Any divergence —
+`[FAIL]` instead of `[INCOMPLETE]`, a nonzero exit, a missing count —
+surfaces as a diff.
+
+## Rebasing onto a newer upstream alcotest
+
+```sh
+git fetch origin
+git checkout <newer-tag>              # e.g. 1.10.0
+git switch qcheck-inc-incomplete      # this branch
+git rebase <newer-tag>                # resolve any conflicts
+dune build                            # verify
+dune runtest test/e2e/alcotest/passing   # verify the e2e guard
+```
+
+Conflicts should be rare and mechanical. The patch is small (~11 lines
+across 4 files under `src/alcotest-engine/`) and adds one variant plus
+a handful of polymorphic-variant branches, so the only routine collision
+source is upstream renumbering lines inside `core.ml` / `model.ml` /
+`pp.ml`.
+
+## Reverting to stock alcotest
+
+Switch back to upstream `main` (or any unpatched ref):
+
+```sh
+git switch main
+dune build
+```
+
+The build succeeds because the patch never introduced any public
+identifier; consumer code that uses only `Alcotest.(check ...)` /
+`test_case` / `run` + `failwith "TODO:..."` still compiles. Behaviourally,
+though:
+
+- Tests raising `Failure "TODO:..."` get the standard `[FAIL]` treatment.
+- Runs exit with code 1 instead of 0 when TODO-tagged tests fire without
+  any real failure.
+
+So the degradation is silent and behavioural, never a build error.
